(Stage 1d — the value-parameter ABI around the 6-register boundary. Test
 165 covers 7 argument words (1 stack word, odd, 8-byte pad); these cover
 8 words (2 stack words, even, no pad), 9 words (3 stack words, odd, pad),
 a value in the FIRST position, and two values in one signature. A wrong
 pad offset or word index shows up as a mistagged or mispaired argument.)

To w8 with a number called aa and a number called b and a number called c and a number called d and a number called e and a number called f and a value called v.
  If v is a text, print "w8 text f={f}".
  Otherwise print "w8 num {v} f={f}".

To w9 with a number called aa and a number called b and a number called c and a number called d and a number called e and a number called f and a number called g and a value called v.
  If v is a text, print "w9 text g={g}".
  Otherwise print "w9 num {v} g={g}".

To vfirst with a value called v and a number called aa and a number called b.
  If v is a text, print "vfirst text b={b}".
  Otherwise print "vfirst num {v} b={b}".

To twovals with a value called v and a number called aa and a value called w.
  If v is a text, print "twovals v-text a={aa}".
  Otherwise print "twovals v-num a={aa}".

w8 of 1 and 2 and 3 and 4 and 5 and 6 and "hi".
w8 of 1 and 2 and 3 and 4 and 5 and 6 and 99.
w9 of 1 and 2 and 3 and 4 and 5 and 6 and 7 and "yo".
w9 of 1 and 2 and 3 and 4 and 5 and 6 and 7 and 88.
vfirst of "aa" and 1 and 2.
vfirst of 77 and 1 and 2.
twovals of "x" and 5 and "y".
twovals of 4 and 5 and 6.
